    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<br><br>Just to clear things up<br>In the documentation the spectral entropy sh is compute with &quot;y = relative amplitude of the i frequency,&quot; (with sum(yi)=1).<br>But in the examples, for instance:<br><br><pre style=\"font-family:monospace\">a<span>&lt;-</span>synth<span style=\"color:#009900\">(</span>f=<span style=\"color:#cc66cc\">8000</span><span style=\"color:#339933\">,</span>d=<span style=\"color:#cc66cc\">1</span><span style=\"color:#339933\">,</span>cf=<span style=\"color:#cc66cc\">2000</span><span style=\"color:#339933\">,</span><a href=\"http://inside-r.org/r-doc/graphics/plot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://inside-r.org/r-doc/graphics/plot&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472290691000&amp;usg=AOvVaw04WgY6BDSeXjuo1kl6vPu0\"><span style=\"color:#003399;font-weight:bold\">plot</span></a>=<span style=\"color:#000000;font-weight:bold\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#009900\">)</span>\nspeca<span>&lt;-</span>spec<span style=\"color:#009900\">(</span>a<span style=\"color:#339933\">,</span>f=<span style=\"color:#cc66cc\">8000</span><span style=\"color:#339933\">,</span>at=<span style=\"color:#cc66cc\">0.5</span><span style=\"color:#339933\">,</span><a href=\"http://inside-r.org/r-doc/graphics/plot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://inside-r.org/r-doc/graphics/plot&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472290691000&amp;usg=AOvVaw04WgY6BDSeXjuo1kl6vPu0\"><span style=\"color:#003399;font-weight:bold\">plot</span></a>=<span style=\"color:#000000;font-weight:bold\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#009900\">)</span>\n<span style=\"color:#666666;font-style:italic\">##########################</span>\n<span style=\"color:#666666;font-style:italic\"># Shannon spectral entropy</span>\n<span style=\"color:#666666;font-style:italic\">##########################</span>\nsh<span style=\"color:#009900\">(</span>speca<span style=\"color:#009900\">)<br></span></pre><br> I don&#39;t see how the spectrum is normalized. So, the sum of the bin does not equal 1. Does it ?<br><br>Could you please clarify that point?<br>Thanks a lot.<br><br>P.G. <br></div>"
    ]
